            unit: "Minister Edren",
            x: 13,
            y: 29,
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_3",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("Prince Haldric has emerged from the sewers of Southbay in the very heart of the city. After some commotion, he gains an audience with the King of Southbay."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("So, Prince, you bring refugees, but do you bring swords as well?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("I bear both, and all are loyal to the King of Southbay!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("I knew you as a boy, and your people have preceded you. Your father was an honorable man, and so are you. Aren’t you the king now?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("A king with no land and no crown is no king, my Lord."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("It is so. These are dark days to live through, my young prince. You’ve done your father proud. Far better than my legacy, a dead adventurer and a missing fool! It is fitting that my line should end with my kingdom."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            portrait: "portraits/haldric-surprised.webp",
            text: _("You should not say such things!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("Hmph! It matters little now. What’s this? You bring a Wesfolk waif with you. Put her out with the others!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("You’ve put my people out in the snow? Prepare to meet your fate you—"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("She and her people have been of great service to me. Open the gates, let them in."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("What? On your word alone, boy? And what of the other Wesfolk that have drifted to our gate?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("Let them all in! For the sake of humanity on this isle!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("And because I can sweeten the deal. I can save the lives of all of the people left on this isle. I will reveal all, if you swear on the soul of your eldest son that you let all of the Wesfolk who may come into the city, and allow them to participate in what must happen next."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("Hmm... Very well. I so swear. Speak."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("First, I <i>can</i> translate the book that will allow Haldric to use the Ruby of Fire. The artifact should help with what must come."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("Second, I know the way to the mysterious lands of the east. Addroran, I was your son’s navigator and companion. Believe me, you must go east."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            portrait: "portraits/haldric-surprised.webp",
            text: _("Compan— What?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Burin the Lost",
            text: _("She’s just full of surprises."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("I was the navigator. Haldric, your people simply washed up here long ago, but my people came here on purpose. You’d all still be herding sheep and living in grass huts if it wasn’t for my people."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("Some favor your people did for us. Why flee at all? And why east? We’ve already repelled one orcish assault. We should be working toward taking back the Isle."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("This is no time for bravado. You must head east because my people came from the west, which is teeming with every form of enemy and monster imaginable. There is literally no room there. If you thought we were bad, you should see what else comes behind us. You’d be slaves, or you’d be dead."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("Learn the lesson of my people. If we had fled here while even one of our great cities still stood we could have taken this Isle with ease. But we fought on until the bitter end. There can be no compromise with the orcs, their numbers are limitless, and you have no way to stop more orcs from coming."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("Hmm. There is wisdom in your words, and my end should be in this place. We can hold out for the rest of the winter here. When the orcs last came it was fall and the harvest was in. We can hunt the great schools of fish that live under the ice. You might even be able to depart in well-provisioned ships!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("Don’t you intend to come with us?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("No. Flee, and flee east. It is my duty to hold this city as long as I can for the sake of all who can be evacuated. That means it shall fall on Haldric and you to lead the evacuation."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("King, there will be a new kingdom in the east, and the bulk of the fleet will bear the flag of Southbay. A new throne and new lands await you in the east."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "King Addroran IX",
            text: _("My bloodline has ended with my sons, and I am old. Let the ships take the women, children, and young men first. A new kingdom must be born of vital blood. We old men are still of some value. We will make the orcs pay dearly when they come to take this place!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("If there is no other way. May the bards forever sing of the valor of the Kings of Southbay! Jessene, about that book?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("I’ll begin my translation. Oh, and you should seal up the sewer entrance."),
          },
          {
            tag: "win",
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
]
